{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,17]],"date-time":"2026-08-17T14:24:58Z","timestamp":1786976698309,"version":"build-2736575974"},"reference-count":64,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"36","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,30]],"date-time":"2023-10-30T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1698624000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/501100001659","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["390677874"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["390677874"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/501100001659","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Advanced Science"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,12]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    Since the birth of the computational hydrogen electrode approach, it is considered that activity trends of electrocatalysts in a homologous series can be quantified by the construction of volcano plots. This method aims to steer materials discovery by the identification of catalysts\u00a0with an improved reaction kinetics, though evaluated by means of thermodynamic descriptors. The conventional approach for the volcano plot of the oxygen evolution reaction (OER)\u00a0relies on the assumption of the mononuclear mechanism, comprising the\n                    <jats:sup>*<\/jats:sup>\n                    OH,\n                    <jats:sup>*<\/jats:sup>\n                    O, and\n                    <jats:sup>*<\/jats:sup>\n                    OOH intermediates. In the present manuscript, two new mechanistic pathways, comprising the idea of the Walden inversion in that bond\u2010breaking and bond\u2010making occurs simultaneously, are factored into a potential\u2010dependent OER activity volcano plot. Surprisingly, it turns out that the Walden inversion plays an important role since the activity volcano is governed by mechanistic pathways comprising Walden steps rather than by the traditionally assumed reaction mechanisms under typical OER conditions.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/advs.202305505","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,31]],"date-time":"2023-10-31T02:18:51Z","timestamp":1698718731000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":38,"title":["Importance of the Walden Inversion for the Activity Volcano Plot of Oxygen Evolution"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"10","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2934-6075","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Kai S.","family":"Exner","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Faculty of Chemistry Theoretical Inorganic Chemistry University Duisburg\u2010Essen  Universit\u00e4tsstra\u00dfe 5 45141 Essen Germany"},{"name":"Cluster of Excellence RESOLV  44801 Bochum Germany"},{"name":"Center for Nanointegration (CENIDE) Duisburg\u2010Essen  47057 Duisburg Germany"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,30]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_7_1_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1126\/science.aat6749"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.ijhydene.2013.01.151"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/advs.202002446"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41560-019-0407-1"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41563-020-0788-3"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1126\/science.aad4998"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/anie.201709652"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_8_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/acscatal.1c01973"},{"key":"